    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d401">

                <pb facs="0406" n="400" sameAs="frus:frus1942v02/pg400"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/24969: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Algiers (Cole) to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Algiers</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-10-20T16:00:00+01:00">October 20, 1942—4
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received October 20—2:32 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>701. From Murphy for Atherton. For Leahy. Admiral Darlan arrived at Oran this
                    morning en route to Dakar for an inspection trip said to be pending for the last
                    2 months. He is expected in Algiers on his return in about 1 week stopping over
                    for about 2 days as the guest of General Juin commanding in North Africa.</p>
                <p>I promised to inquire discreetly whether American specialists might have helpful
                    suggestions to offer regarding treatment of poliomyelitis. Could possibly
                    Admiral McIntire<anchor n="98" xml:id="d401-f1"/> cable me confidentially
                    anything that might be useful. [Murphy.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cole</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d401-f1" n="98" xml:id="d401-f1-content">
                <p>Vice Adm. Ross T. McIntire, White House physician.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
